<!--Post: 3958--><!--Time: 1105451670-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3958"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 5:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think the story today on Kansas.com states the way the police would handle the gathering of dna from a suspect in the BTK investigation. They are not going to pussyfoot around! Waiting for someone to slip up or break down. The Green River Killer  Gary Ridgeway was asked years ago for a DNA sample and submitted to one. Thats how they got enough for an arrest warrent in that case. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3958-->
<!--Post: 3960--><!--Time: 1105452258-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3960"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 6:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->But its all about voulenteering your DNA. It takes a court order with probable cause. No DA in the county would risk jeopardizing the entire investigation on a whim. They need him to slip up. He&#39;s been at this game for years, it&#39;s the WPD&#39;s only hope.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3960-->
<!--Post: 3962--><!--Time: 1105468030-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3962"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Luvmysteries<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Luvmysteries<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 10:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Could not the WPD have had this suspect in for an informal interview &#40;I believe they have talked to him previously&#41;? During that interview could they not have offered him a cup of coffee and then let him go? His coffee cup would have been &#34;thrown away.&#34; Instead, you have fingerprints and DNA. Just a thought.......<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3962-->
<!--Post: 3979--><!--Time: 1105498623-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3979"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 6:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The man in the story on Kansas.com states he was told they where going to take a DNA sample from him one way or another. He says his dna was taken <BR>but he did not submit to it. So take that for what it is. The police arrested him for another offense but the real reason was because he was a BTK suspect. Personally I approve of the way the police acted in this case, they must of had something to act the way they did. In this case in didn&#39;t pan out but in the future if they let this change their tactics, they may lose a chance to catch the real BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3979-->
<!--Post: 3984--><!--Time: 1105500614-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3984"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 7:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another interesting clue as to why I think they <BR>have zeroed in a suspect was the Police Chief&#39;s <BR>words at his year-end briefing, when he said, <BR>&#34;this is a very thorough, systematic and patient <BR>investigation.&#34;  Those are very well-chosen <BR>adjectives, especially since the arrest debacle of early December.  It is as through they do have a suspect, but are going to be extremely &#34;thorough and systematic&#34; in their data gathering, research and surveillance.  But the last word, &#34;patient&#34;, is a big clue - they are taking their time, and getting every bit of information all lined up.  They are not going to make a rush to judgment like the earlier BTK suspect.  I think they realized what havoc it wreaks upon the other family members, society, - and an innocent who is wrongly accused.  This time, when a BTK suspect is arrested, they want to make sure it&#39;s the real thing.  Therefore, extra time alloted for positive identification will be well worth the effort.  <BR>And, also, if he is being surveilled, they could possibly catch him in the act of making the &#34;anniversary drop&#34; on the 15th.  Any thoughts?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3984-->
<!--Post: 3988--><!--Time: 1105502476-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3988"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 8:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->CURIOUS2 wrote: &#34;Another interesting clue as to why I think they have zeroed in a suspect was the Police Chief&#39;s words at his year-end briefing, when he said, &#34;this is a very thorough, systematic and patient investigation.&#34; <BR> <BR>Don&#39;t forget, CURIOUS2, that is ALSO the behavior of a police department that HAS ABSOLUTELY NO CLUE as to who the BLT is. They are probably no closer now that they were 30 years ago. It sounds to me exactly like they are just &#34;twiddling their thumbs&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3988-->
<!--Post: 3990--><!--Time: 1105503305-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3990"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 8:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If they have a suspect upon whom they&#39;ve zeroed in, DNA can be obtained from his garbage or the like. Also, if the suspect knows he&#39;s been singled out, he&#39;s partially captured in that he&#39;d be under surveillance and this means he isn&#39;t going to kill anyone else. BTK would also have a heck of a time making drops, too. If there is another BTK drop, I doubt he&#39;s yet been zeroed in upon.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3990-->
<!--Post: 3991--><!--Time: 1105504130-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3991"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 8:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Curious2, it&#39;s possible WPD is acting under advisement from other agencies, such as KBI or FBI. During the suburban Washington, DC sniper murders, Chief Moose was technically &#34;in charge,&#34; but much of what he said was being written by others outside his department. That said, I know BTK isn&#39;t the same thing, but others outside WPD <i>may</i> be partially responsible for the contents of WPD&#39;s press conferences. Or maybe not. <BR> <BR>It&#39;s just a likely that Victor&#39;s correct. Let&#39;s see what happens on January 15. Let&#39;s see if there&#39;s a drop.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3991-->
<!--Post: 3992--><!--Time: 1105504463-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3992"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 8:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, VS.  I guess what I was trying to say <BR>is that I don&#39;t feel the WPD was very &#34;thorough, <BR>systematic or patient&#34; when they arrested Valadez <BR>last month. So, to me, when the Chief used those 3 adjectives, they almost sounded as though they were directed toward one specific suspect.  And, George, wouldn&#39;t WPD be surveilling suspect in order to catch him in the act of the drop?  That would be much better than barging in on his home like with Valadez.  What do you think?  Thanks for your insights!  Also, why don&#39;t you think <BR>WPD is staging any more random swabbings?  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3992-->
<!--Post: 3999--><!--Time: 1105515878-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3999"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 11:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wish some one smart like George could find the legal guidlines for DNA legality. They just cant dig thu your trash and get a sample. They cant just take you DNS fom a cup. Now it could be a helpful tool to get an idea if your after the right suspect. But the evidence collected by such means will never stand in a cout of law.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3999-->
<!--Post: 4000--><!--Time: 1105516215-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4000"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 11:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Or I have a better idea. Just classify BTK as a domestic terrorist and then all suspects will fall under the Patriot Act, then they can just arrest you with no proof, take you DNA with out a court order, hold any suspects as long as they want, and if they arrest the wrong people they can release them without the embarrasment of making a mistake. Why? They would be fighting a terrorist. Just kidding....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4000-->
<!--Post: 4001--><!--Time: 1105519468-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4001"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 12:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>They just cant dig thu your trash and get a sample.</i> <BR>To the best of my knowledge they can, and they need no warrant, at least not for dumpsters used by apartments or trash placed in any public setting. Or maybe I&#39;m wrong. If so, then that&#39;s that.  <BR> <BR>Nugzter, you obviously have an agenda and seem unusually interersted in me. Please leave me alone, and stop attacking me. I did nothing to warrant this foul-mouthed attack from you: <i>&#34;Think about it, Billy Bob dumb a&#42;&#42; send the cop to the library to look for a specific book by Dewwy decimal. He has to had &#34;knowledge&#34; of this library. He is not some loser guy who cant read. Come on George&#34;</i> <b>so please stop it.</b> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4001-->
<!--Post: 4002--><!--Time: 1105520440-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4002"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 1:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dear George, It wasnt an attack on you. It was just an answer to your question. Dont be too over sensitive. Now about your I cant spell refrence in the other thread. That was more like an attack. But I dont complain. By the way I got 3 keys on my work PC that dont always wok. The keys are: R, E, S. So get over it. I got nothing against you. Just disagree with your theorys.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4002-->
<!--Post: 4003--><!--Time: 1105524795-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4003"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 2:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>&#34;Now about your I cant spell refrence in the other thread. That was more like an attack. But I dont complain.&#34;</i> <BR>Actually, it was a response to your foul-mouthed attack upon me, as quoted above; you now say, of your attack, &#34;it was just an answer to your question.&#34; Scroll up for two consecutive posts which are other attacks on me. It really doesn&#39;t matter what you think of my opinions but it&#39;s no excuse for the tone, sarcasm and foul-language you&#39;ve been using toward me. Please stop it. Have you been able to find the link you mentioned about the five police officers who refused to give DNA samples? I&#39;m interested in reading about that. <BR> <BR>Curious2, Yes, I agree with you about the surveillance. The police either have the guy or they have ten pounds of air. January 15 will be  interesting; we&#39;ll see if there&#39;s a drop or communication by BTK. It seems clear he knows Wichita very well.  <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4003-->
<!--Post: 4004--><!--Time: 1105527691-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4004"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 3:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m still looking for the link. But I&#39;m at work and have no time at the moment. It is somewhere here on this site too in another thread. Its just a matter of time til I find it. If you have time to look someone has posted it. If not I&#39;ll continue. <BR>Now the Billy Bob dumb a&#42;&#42; coment was not pointed at you. It was in refrence to BTK not being a dumb a&#42;&#42;. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4004-->
<!--Post: 4005--><!--Time: 1105528427-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4005"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 3:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Courious2 is correct. Thats the best way to catch him. I believe the tactic is to even make the surveillance obvious to the suspect. WPD &#40;if they do have a hot suspect&#41; are surely making it obvious that the suspect is being tracked. That really turns on the heat for a suspect, then he may mess up and do something out of the ordinary. Like give up, strike a deal with the DA, and sit his few remaining years gloating. Look at Green River. Perfect example. BTK is very well studied on all types of serial killers, He is surely familiar with the Green River outcome, and has more than likely comtomplated this avenue of surender.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4005-->
<!--Post: 4007--><!--Time: 1105530475-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4007"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 3:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nugzter, cool! If you&#39;re at work, I&#39;ll look for the link later in the morning. I have to step out in a minute myself. It may tie in with Curious2&#39;s swab question, which I&#39;d like to answer but am not sure how to! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4007-->
<!--Post: 4010--><!--Time: 1105533586-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4010"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Curious2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Curious2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 4:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Nugzter and George - thanks for your thoughts! <BR>But until WPD obtain a warrant for suspect&#39;s <BR>DNA, wouldn&#39;t they do like George said, and just <BR>dig through the guy&#39;s trash to get an &#34;unofficial <BR>and prelimimary&#34; sample?  I&#39;m predicting it all happens this weekend - just an intuitive nudge.  Hey Nugzter, do you think WPD would let the suspect know he&#39;s being tracked?  What you said <BR>makes sense though - to &#34;turn up the heat&#34; <BR>so that he can make mistakes.  But I would think <BR>they would be more secretive about surveillance. <BR>I appreciate both of your comments. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4010-->
<!--Post: 4017--><!--Time: 1105538606-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4017"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 6:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thx Curious and George, <BR>I&#39;ll use an example of what I mentioned before. <BR>An aquaintance of mine was suspected of stealing cars. They invited him for an interview and just asked him some questions. He was purchased a can of Dr. Pepper and left it sitting on the desk where the interview was done. <BR>Sure enough next thing he knew, the police were parking down the street tailing his every move. About after 3 or 4 days he got tired of it and just walked over to the car and they took off. Months went by and he was so paranoid, kept seeing the cars following him and parked down his street. Finally he called his lawyer and made a deal. The pints on the can were a match, but were never taken thru popper procedure. Were never even mentioned in court. He got something like 12 years reduced to 6. And the poliece had no real poof he did it &#40;got a tip fom ex gf&#41;. <BR>But he confessed. No proof needed. Now dont quote me on this. I got this info second hand from my brother and I live in Germany for the last 15 years. But look at Seven, they put the heat on and Kevin Spacey tued himself in after they were on to him. <BR>I&#39;m gonna start looking for that link now. Give me a few.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4017-->
<!--Post: 4050--><!--Time: 1105576243-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4050"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cranium<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cranium<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 4:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I testified for the prosecution in a murder case.  This man raped and murdered a woman, but they obtained the physical evidence illegally, so they had to let him go.  The victim was a homicide detective&#39;s daughter.  They were unable to go after him for this murder, until he raped a girl about three years later.  They were able to use the physical evidence from the rape to reopen the murder case against him.  Now, I could be wrong about things, but it seems to me that if they could have just pulled a used razor out of the trash or whatever, the murder victim&#39;s father would have done it. Maybe the laws vary from state to state.  This was in Oklahoma.  I would be curious to see someone with a legal background expand on this subject. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4050-->
<!--Post: 4067--><!--Time: 1105633599-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4067"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 8:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whoisbtk, you have any valuable insights to this one?  I tend to agree with the idea that they could get the evidence &#34;illegally&#34; for the matter of eliminating suspects, but if there were a match, they&#39;d have to pretend they never acquired it in the first place.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4067-->
<!--Post: 4068--><!--Time: 1105636741-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4068"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 9:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;ll take an experienced criminal trial lawyer who knows both Kansas and possibly Federal law. Because the FBI is involved, my guess is that in combination with WPD and KBI, they won&#39;t blow the case as concerns physical evidence. <b>It&#39;s WPD&#39;s case, I hope it stays that way.</b> But we need a lawyer to explain things, as we can speculate till the cows come home.  <BR> <BR>What we need most of all is a suspect.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4068-->
<!--Post: 4073--><!--Time: 1105644143-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4073"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 11:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree. Its a tactic that will absolutly work. B´TK also wants it to stay in the hands of WPD. They are his rival. I bet when it all comes out &#40;if it ever does&#41; he had some sort of grudge against WPD. An arrest when he was a teen, some sort of bad contact with the police. Maybe the railroad detective his mom supposedly was in a relationship with.  <BR>I saw a lecture from a professior from Vienna on sexual serial killers. And it caused me to think more about his background. I`m sure he fits the pattern of all sexual murders. Hes a neat freak. <BR>He also has diffrent levels of sexaul fantasy. Some softer, some in the middle, and the ultimate.Sometimes when he killed, it is more than likly he may have had a soft, or middle fantasy, that built itsself up to a really brutal ending. Still would like to know what he did to the bodies post mortum, besides maybe pose them for pics in his collection. That would explain alot about his &#34;normal&#34; every day personality. He is also a liar. The only moment of truth is when he commits his crimes. Other than that hes a shifty liar. And I bet it is obvious to his immediate family. Especialy in his older years. People change and the mind starts to go. I would say he loses control alot more lately. Hes bound to slip up. So if the WPD does have a susspect that they may have obtained DNA from, by what ever means, this is the time to start looking. They should have him by March. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4073-->
<!--Post: 4180--><!--Time: 1105839190-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4180"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jim44095<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jim44095<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 15, 2005 - 5:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was just wondering if BTK had been seeing an Psychiatrist,and maybe that person was able to keep his urges under control and that person may have died and now he  is out of control again. <BR>In the letter that was publicized 11months after the first killings he makes a suggestion about being psychotic but not being able to tell anyone for fear they would go to the police.Did he eventually find a shrink who would not violate client dr privledges? <BR> <BR>The article I&#39;m referring to is at this link <BR><a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolved/btk/them_3.html?sect=4" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolve d/btk/them_3.html?sect=4</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4180-->
<!--Post: 7416--><!--Time: 1108488294-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7416"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 9:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It is popular belief that all serial killers kill throughout their lives and if they stop killing, that they must have an overwhelming reason to quit. Reasons like being imprisoned, or in a hospital, or abroad, etc...  <BR> <BR>I was reading a new serial killer site &#40;imagine that - a website dedicated exclusively to  all serial killers&#41;, where it shows that MOST serial killers attain a certain &#34;number&#34; of victims and then they stop. Those are the ones who are the most difficult to catch. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.serial-killer.org/index.php" target=_top>http://www.serial-killer.org/index.php</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7416-->
</table></td></tr></table>
